  "body": "The spec says:\r\n\r\n    [dir=ltr i], [dir=rtl i], [dir=auto i] {\r\n      unicode-bidi: isolate; \r\n    }\r\n\r\nin the rendering section.  As far as I can tell (by testing `<span dir>` and `<span dir=\"spork\">`, both Chrome and Firefox implement:\r\n\r\n    [dir] { unicode-bidi: isolate; }\r\n\r\ninstead.  Safari has:\r\n\r\n    [dir] { unicode-bidi: embed; }\r\n\r\nEdge has, afaict:\r\n\r\n    [dir=ltr i], [dir=rtl i] {\r\n      unicode-bidi: embed; \r\n    }\r\n\r\nwhich is closest to what the spec has, and in particular treats invalid values like the spec does.\r\n\r\nI'm considering aligning Gecko with the spec, but would like to know whether other UAs are willing to do that too before I start changing behavior...\r\n\r\n//cc @domenic ",
